event('190-B1-lemma1.1','targeted proof check','Write B=A-prime and C^n=B^(tensor n+1) tensor M with differential the alternating insertion of 1. After faithfully flat extension A to B the new algebra B tensor_A B has the retraction multiplication. In the split case with retraction e:B to A, h_n(b0 tensor ... tensor bn tensor m)=e(b0)b1 tensor ... tensor bn tensor m (and h_0(b0 tensor m)=e(b0)m) satisfies dh+hd=id by cancellation of adjacent insertion terms, including the augmentation. Faithful flatness detects the homology groups, proving the stated resolution.','190, p. 316, lemma 1.1 and proof')
event('190-B1-theorem1-proof','targeted proof check','The affine full-faithfulness assertion follows by applying Hom_A(M,-) to the equalizer N to B tensor N double-arrow B tensor B tensor N supplied by lemma 1.1; no finiteness hypothesis on M is needed because Hom preserves equalizers. For effectivity, express a descent datum on a B-module N as a map delta:N to B tensor_A N, B-linear for the first factor, with multiplication composed with delta equal to id and (id tensor delta)delta(n)=sum b_i tensor 1 tensor n_i when delta(n)=sum b_i tensor n_i. Let M={n:delta(n)=1 tensor n}. Flatness identifies B tensor M with the corresponding kernel in B tensor N; the displayed cocycle identity puts delta(N) in this kernel. Delta and multiplication B tensor M to N are inverse, yielding the descended module. On affine opens of S, quasi-compactness gives a finite affine cover of S-prime whose disjoint union is affine and faithfully flat over S. Ordinary sheaf gluing over that cover and over affine opens of S yields the global assertion. This supplies the equalizer construction suppressed in the brief printed reduction to the split case.','190, p. 316, proof of theorem 1(i),(ii)')
event('190-B1-corollary1','used and rechecked in this run','Putting F=O_S in full faithfulness identifies compatible Hom maps with sections in the displayed equalizer. Both labeled arrows p1-star and p2-star have the printed rightward orientation; the first arrow is alpha-star.','190, pp. 315–316, corollary 1')
event('190-B1-corollary2','targeted proof check','A submodule sheaf of G-prime whose two pullbacks agree inherits the restricted canonical descent datum, including its cocycle identity. Effectivity descends it and full faithfulness descends its inclusion into G. Faithfully flat pullback reflects injectivity, so the descended morphism is a subobject. Conversely any subobject pulls back to such an invariant subobject, and full faithfulness gives uniqueness. Quotients follow by the same exactness argument.','190, p. 316, corollary 2')
event('190-B1-lemma1.1-corollary','used and rechecked in this run','Taking M=A in the checked augmented resolution gives H0=A and Hi=0 for every i>=1. These are additive-group cohomology groups, as printed.','190, p. 316, unnumbered corollary')
